{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you came near to me, all of you.</b> In disorder (בְּעִרְבּוּבְיָא). And further on it says (Deuteronomy 5), ״וַתִּקְרְבוּן אֵלַי כָּל רָאשֵׁי שִׁבְטֵיכֶם וְזִקְנֵיכֶם וַתֹּאמְרוּ הֵן הֶרְאָנוּ״ וגו׳ — that coming near was proper: the young honoring the elders and sending them ahead, and the elders honoring the heads to go ahead; but here, ״וַתִּקְרְבוּן אֵלַי כֻּלְּכֶם״ in disorder — the young shoving the elders, and the elders shoving the heads (Sifrei)." "<b>And they returned word to us.</b> In what manner did they speak?" "<b>The road by which we shall go up.</b> There is no road without its twists." "<b>And the cities to which we shall come.</b> First, to conquer (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:30.195187729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}